cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  ProxMPC: Nonlinear Model Predictive Control for ROS 2, as a
  reusable core and a Nav2 controller plugin
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Simone
    family-names: Contorno
    email: simone.contorno@outlook.it
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0002-4187-2166'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/simone-contorno/prox_mpc'
abstract: >-
  ProxMPC solves the nonlinear optimal-control problem with a Sequential
  Quadratic Programming scheme over the ProxQP solver, packaged as a reusable
  C++ core and a Nav2 controller plugin for ROS 2 Jazzy. Obstacles enter the
  optimisation as linearised signed-distance half-planes with a discrete-time
  Control Barrier Function coupling, making keep-out a hard constraint rather
  than a cost penalty. The repository also provides a lidar obstacle tracker
  based on an Interacting Multiple Model filter (constant-velocity and
  constant-turn-rate), a Gazebo Harmonic demonstration, and a benchmarking
  harness that compares the controller against the stock Nav2 local controllers
  under matched speed caps, prediction horizons, and perception.
keywords:
  - robotics
  - ROS 2
  - Nav2
  - model predictive control
  - nonlinear optimisation
  - motion planning
  - obstacle avoidance
  - mobile robots
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-07-19'
references:
  - type: software
    title: 'ProxSuite: a scalable and efficient QP solver'
    abstract: The QP solver ProxMPC builds each control cycle's sub-problem for.
    authors:
      - name: The Simple-Robotics team, INRIA
    repository-code: 'https://github.com/Simple-Robotics/proxsuite'
